<title>USA: IBM unveils low-power chip for network PCs.</title>
<headline>IBM unveils low-power chip for network PCs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp Monday unveiled a chip designed to power network computers and other digital devices, the company said.</p>
<p>IBM's PowerPC 403GCX chip is a low-power, high-performace chip that integrates functions such as data and memory management, thereby cutting manufacturing costs, the firm said.</p>
<p>The chip is available in speeds of 50 and 66 megahertz, for $37 and $44.50 per unit, respectively, in 10,000 unit quantities.</p>
